Prepare enough records to demonstrate page sizes  10 ,  20 ,  50 , and  100 . Audit results are scoped to the currently selected tenant and business unit.

────────────────────

Presenter talk track

1. Introduce the page

Action

1. Log in to RGS Admin Portal.
2. Select the required tenant and business unit.
3. Open Audit Log from the sidebar.

Say

The Audit Log provides a tenant- and business-unit-scoped history of actions performed in the portal. Records are displayed newest first and include the user, action, result, source page, and audit entry ID.

Verify

• Breadcrumb displays Home > Audit Log.
• Search form spans the available content width.
• Result table shows:
• Date Time
• User ID (Email)
• Audit Entry ID
• Action Type
• Action/Activity
• Action Result
• Page

────────────────────

3. Search by user email

Action

1. Enter  admin@example.com  in User ID (Email).
2. Click Search.

Say

Audit records can be filtered by the user who performed the action.

Expected result

• Only records matching  admin@example.com  appear.
• Total record count is updated.
• Results remain sorted by newest date first.
• Pagination returns to page 1.

────────────────────

4. Search by action type

Action

1. Click Clear.
2. Select Create from Action Type.
3. Click Search.

Say

Standard action categories include Login, Logout, Create, Update, Read, Delete, Export, Download, and Status Change.

Expected result

• Only Create actions are shown.
• Successful results have a green Success tag.
• Failed results, if present, have a red Fail tag.

────────────────────

5. Search by activity

Action

1. Click Clear.
2. Enter  Create Consent  in Action/Activity.
3. Press Enter instead of clicking Search.

Say

Users can also search by the business activity name. Text searches can be submitted directly with Enter.

Expected result

• Matching Create Consent records appear.
• Each result includes its unique Audit Entry ID and originating page.

────────────────────

6. Combined filtering

Action

Apply all of the following:

• User ID:  admin@example.com 
• Action Type:  Create 
• Action/Activity:  Create Consent 
• Date From / Date To: a range containing the prepared record

Click Search.

Say

Filters can be combined to narrow the investigation to a specific user, action, activity, and date range.

Expected result

• Every displayed record satisfies all selected criteria.
• Date/time is displayed as  DD/MM/YYYY HH:mm:ss .
• The date filter includes the entire From and To dates.

────────────────────

7. Demonstrate validation

No search parameters

Action

1. Click Clear.
2. Click Search without entering anything.

Expected message

Please provide at least one search parameter.

Incomplete date range

Action

1. Select only Date From.
2. Click Search.

Expected message

Both 'Date From' and 'Date To' are required when using date range.

Invalid date order

Action

1. Select a Date From later than Date To.
2. Click Search.

Expected message

'Date From' cannot be later than 'Date To'.

Say

Client-side validation prevents broad accidental searches and invalid date-range requests.

────────────────────

8. No-result behavior

Action

1. Click Clear.
2. Enter a nonexistent user such as  unknown.demo@example.com .
3. Click Search.

Expected result

• Table displays:

No activities found matching your search criteria.

• Page remains usable.
• No stale results from the previous search remain visible.

────────────────────

9. Clear and reset

Action

1. Click Clear after applying several filters.

Expected result

• All input fields reset.
• Validation messages disappear.
• Current page resets to page 1.
• Default page size returns to the current configured state.
• Initial audit records are requested again.

────────────────────

10. Pagination

Action

1. Search for a criterion returning more than ten records.
2. Navigate to page 2.
3. Change page size from  10  to  20 , then optionally  50 .

Say

Pagination supports 10, 20, 50, or 100 records per page while preserving the active filters.

Expected result

• Summary displays, for example:

Showing 11 – 20 of 37 records

• Filters remain active while paging.
• Changing page size updates the result range correctly.

────────────────────

11. Tenant/business-unit isolation

Action

1. Note the current Audit Log results.
2. Change the selected tenant or business unit.
3. Return to Audit Log and repeat the same search.

Say

Audit records are always restricted to the active tenant and business-unit context. Users cannot retrieve audit events belonging to another context through this page.

Expected result

• Results reflect only the newly selected context.
• Records from the previous tenant/business unit do not appear.

